<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of London (1718)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1718">1718</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Quadruple Alliance (1718) · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-quadruple-alliance">War of the Quadruple Alliance</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Quadruple Alliance was formed in 1718 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> expected to join, to uphold the Peace of Utrecht against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, which had seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-quadruple-alliance">War of the Quadruple Alliance</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-the-hague-1720">Treaty of The Hague</a> of 1720 gave Sicily to Austria and Sardinia to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-amadeus-ii">Victor Amadeus II</a> of Savoy, and promised Parma and Tuscany to Philip V's son Charles.</p></div>
